r was very closely linked to  advances in transportation  first it was having rail cars and  automobiles that could get flowers from  farms to markets  and then it was airplanes to get them  from warm climates to cold climates  on thursday the last of the valentine's  day flowers were flown in  and processed at miami international  airport  the stems thoroughly inspected at  customs  amir pineda oversees the operation about  1.1 billion stems of flowers come  through  from the beginning of january through  february 15th  before continuing on to floors and  distributors around the country  all planned planted and primed for one  peak day  february 14th how difficult is it to  make sure that timing is just  right when we're bringing the flowers in  from the farms  we have ethylene gas inhibitors in there  to make sure that the gases  mix is proper for the flowers so there's  so much of a science that goes into this  i thought i was getting into a flower  business running one star  and then getting into this virtual  e-commerce business  what we've had to learn about logistics  and distribution of perishable products  has just been fascinating  the mccann family started with a single  flower shop in new york 45 years ago  before centering their brand  around 1 800 flowers as toll-free  numbers  took off now more than 5 000 of  america's finest florists have the same  telephone number  1 800 flowers then another game changer  so we started to dabble in e-commerce  back in 1991  with a platform i don't know if anyone  still remembers compuserve  we were the first merchant to sell any  product of any kind on aol in 1994.  taking that through the 2000s we just  rode the wave of e-commerce  their flowers now come from partner  farms as well as a network of 5  thousand floors nationwide the company  has expanded across 15 brands of gifts  including carrie and david in the  popcorn factory delivering to 160  countries  it hasn't always been a bed of roses  customer complaints about delayed  deliveries  and bouquets far from what their  pictures promised  have made the rounds on social media  things that didn't really show up  like they were advertised what went  wrong and when you're dealing with a  perishable product  sometimes you're going to have  challenges weather can pose a challenge  both extreme cold extreme heat composer  challenge  but the key is how we respond to that  and when you look at how customers are  reaching us these days  it's through social media we respond to  those messages on  social media within three to five  minutes on average  mccann points to that customer service  as their competitive edge  they also enterprise new concepts like  roses that last a year  and partnerships with celebrities like  fashion designer jason wu  constant innovation and a long tradition  where does the idea of gifting flowers  for valentine's day come from  because valentine's day is in february  it's not the easiest time to give  somebody flowers so  originally originally we sent paper  cards but it really wasn't until  greenhouse technology came along and  made it possible to make flowers bloom  in february  that that migrated over into valentine's  day and that was kind of the 1920s  steward says the idea of gifting  bouquets dates back to the ancient  romans  but the victorians in particular  embraced the language of flowers  using specific blooms to convey careful  messages  they couldn't otherwise sail out some of  those notes  endure today part of it is just  tradition it's really just embedded  in our um in our cultural awareness  there's not a culture anywhere in the  world that doesn't view flowers as this  kind of  romantic way of expressing a sentiment  and those feelings of affection are only  heightened  this valentine's day as we hold the  people we love  closer than ever at least in our hearts  if not always in person how do you think  this valentine's day is going to stack  up in the history of valentine's day's  4 1 800 flowers well in the history  books this valentine's day will  certainly have an asterisk as being a  very different one and we think it's one  of the most important valentine's days  about korea a day that's the culmination  of an incredible year-long  effort encompassing the work of many for  a simple message  between two for cbs this morning  saturday  nancy chen new york very nice  and i believe at the top of the show or  during promo you questioned whether  we were going to get you flowers whether  i was going to get you flowers i think  it's from youtube  i will say yes that's true it was a team  effort but let me  shout out to denia who prepared these  for you  and as you take them home you guys i'm  sure you know this already but cut the  stems before you put them in the vase  and use flower food they're beautiful  right well you know it's  funny i've been to otavalo in ecuador  and  my husband bought me a 24  pack of flowers actually  that's two dozen yes guess how much he  paid for him  a buck  it really is it's the markups incredible  by the way sean grandy not off the hook  you're not off the hook still  valentine's day tomorrow that's all i'm  saying

